---
layout: changelog
title: "Use native request and response objects in Appwrite Functions"
date: 2026-11-24
cover: /images/blog/announcing-native-request-response/cover.avif
tags: functions
---

Every function runtime now passes its web server's request to your code as [`context.req.raw`](/docs/products/functions/develop#native-request). It's a Fetch API `Request` in Node.js 18 and later, Bun, and Deno, an aiohttp `web.Request` in Python, a shelf `Request` in Dart, and the server's own request type in every other runtime. Node.js 18 and later, Bun, Deno, Python, and Dart functions can also [return a native response](/docs/products/functions/develop#native-response) instead of calling a `context.res` method.

```js
export default async ({ req }) => {
    const form = await req.raw.formData();

    return new Response(`Hello, ${form.get('name')}!`);
};
```

Frameworks built on the Fetch API, such as Hono, also run in a JavaScript function without an adapter. `context.req` and the `context.res` methods work as before.

